name>NAKASHIMA, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAMOTO, HIROMI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A novel polythiophene in which the backbone shows intensive absorption in the ultraviolet to visible regions and the polymer chain by itself has optical activity, characterized by comprising, as repeating units, thiophene rings which have a chiral substituent and are represented by general formula (I) (wherein R1 and R2 are the same or different and each represents hydrogen or an organic group, provided that at least one thereof represents enantiopure alkyl having a branch in the  beta -position; and n, indicating the number of repeating units, is 10 to 100,000).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un nouveau polythiophène dont la structure fait preuve d'une absorption intense dans l'ultraviolet dans des zones visibles. La chaîne polymère présente en soi une activité optique caractérisée en ce qu'elle comprend des unités de répétition, des cycles de thiophène ayant un substituant chiral de formule générale (I) dans laquelle R1 et R2 sont identiques ou différents et chacun désigne un hydrogène ou un groupe organique, à condition qu'au moins l'un désigne un alkyle énantiopure ayant un chaînon en position  beta ; et n, indiquant le nombre d'unités de répétition, désigne une valeur comprise entre 10 et 100.000.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org